8f4e/v1

includes
; @pos -37 10
include std/events/risingEdge
includesEnd

note
; @pos 0 -110
; @config export.fileName gridsPatterns
; @config audioRuntime.enabled true
; @config audioRuntime.sampleRate 48000
; @config audioRuntime.audioOutBufferLAddress audioout:buffer
; @config audioRuntime.audioOutBufferRAddress audioout:buffer
; @config bin.kick.url https://static.8f4e.com/assets/samples/808-kick-48khz-s16le.pcm
; @config bin.kick.memory kick:buffer
; @config bin.snare.url https://static.8f4e.com/assets/samples/808-snare-48khz-s16le.pcm
; @config bin.snare.memory snare:buffer
; @config bin.hihat.url https://static.8f4e.com/assets/samples/808-hihat-48khz-s16le.pcm
; @config bin.hihat.memory hiHat:buffer

Mutable Instruments Grids patterns

25 patterns with 32 steps each.
One row per step; columns are
bass drum (BD), snare drum (SD),
and hi-hat / percussion (HH).
Values are rhythmic importance
levels in the range 0 to 255.

Each patternNN matches node_N
in the original source.
Modules are arranged in numeric
order, from left to right,
in a 5 by 5 grid.

Open the grids group to inspect
the patterns. Its trigger input
is connected to the root clock.
The clock produces eight pulses
per beat at the selected tempo.

X and Y blend nearby patterns
using the original drum map.
All five controls range from
0 to 255. Density zero mutes
that channel; higher values
include weaker rhythmic steps.
The BD, SD and HH outputs pulse
once per triggered step.
Step numbers run from 0 to 31.

Kick, snare and hi-hat outputs
trigger three one-shot players.
Each hit restarts its sample.
The mixer sets their levels.

The players load clean 808 kick,
snare and closed hi-hat samples.
Samples are mono, 48 kHz, signed
16-bit little-endian PCM.

Converted to vertical packed
integer rows on 2026-11-01.
